[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its own table says
otherwise. The reports in it describe more than one problem, and one fix to the parser closes
only some of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket now. The parser fix does not close the other two.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and these tenants write the day
  first. The day and month swap: 4 March becomes 3 April. This is the fix that is queued.
- **`hint`**: tenants on `booking-v3` show `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Their people type
  month first, as the hint asks, and the form reads it day first, the tenant's way. The day and
  month swap too, but the parser fix does not touch it: the hint has to change.
- **`one-day`**: the date is read right and lands one day early. A client in Lisbon got Tuesday
  and a client in Toronto got Monday for the same meeting; June bookings alone were off by a
  day. That is a time-zone shift when a date is shown, not a month/day swap. The desk had already
  noted these reports, then filed them under `parser` because of their tenant.

## Why it merged as one

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. Every one
  of these problems arrives as "wrong day" or "wrong date", so the subject cannot tell them apart.
- Intake's tag comes from the reporter's browser, not the tenant. Every `en-US` browser was tagged
  `hint`, whatever tenant or channel it came from, so the tags counted the wrong reports as `hint`.
- The ticket export repeats reports across pages. Counted by id, the rows give the same total
  as the desk.

